From 20a858a6fdd5d0346c980394823fb81c67e123c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 05:28:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): the discard question is waited for

In the desktop app, File > Open and File > New threw away unsaved
changes without asking. tauri-plugin-dialog replaces window.confirm
with an asynchronous one, so the synchronous check saw a Promise
(truthy) and went ahead; and the shell had never granted
dialog:allow-message, so the plugin's dialog could not have shown.
confirmDiscard is asynchronous now and awaited at its three call sites
(Open, New, an empty SketchUp file opening as a new model). On the
desktop it asks through the plugin (askYesNo in src/io/files.ts, with
the app's name on the dialog); in the browser through window.confirm
as before. capabilities/default.json grants dialog:allow-message.

Tests: files.test.ts (the browser asks with window.confirm; the desktop
asks through the plugin and waits), files.spec.ts (the desktop's
asynchronous confirm stood in: Open and New over unsaved changes wait
for No and keep the model, and go ahead on Yes; fails before this fix).

Found on Linux (the 0.1.0-alpha.4 .deb and AppImage, and main) by
scripting the app under Xvfb.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
